.TH WINLN 1 "2 Apr 2013" "winln 1.3 (cygutils)" "Cygutils"
.SH NAME
winln \- create a Windows symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B winln
.RB [\-\fBsvfdFA\fP]
.RB \fITARGET\fP\ \fILINKNAME\fP
.br
.B winln
.RB [\-\fBsvfdFA\fP]
.RB \fITARGET\fP
.br
.B winln
.RB [\-\fBsvfdFA\fP]
.RB \fITARGET...\fP\ \fIDIRECTORY\fP
.br
.B winln
.RB [\-\fBsvfdFA\fP]    
.RB \-t\ \fIDIRECTORY\fP\ \fITARGET...\fP
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B winln
is a drop-in replacement for ln(1), the difference being that
.B winln
creates Windows symbolic links instead of Cygwin ones.
Note that Windows has two kinds of symbolic links: file
links and directory links.
.B winln
automatically chooses the correct type of link when the target exists,
but if the target does not exist, you may want to explicitly specify
the kind of link to create.  Links to non-existent targets default to
file links.
.SH OPTIONS

.TP
\fB\-s\fP, \fB\-\-symbolic\fP
Create a symbolic (as opposed to hard) link.
For compatibility with ln(1),
creating hard links is the default.

.TP
\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-verbose\fP
Print to standard output the names of links created.

.TP
\fB\-f\fP, \fB\-\-force\fP
Replace existing destination file.

.TP
\fB\-d\fP, \fB\-\-directory\fP
Create a directory symbolic link.

.TP
\fB\-F\fP, \fB\-\-file\fP
Create a file symbolic link.

.TP
\fB\-A\fP, \fB\-\-auto\fP
Automatically determine the type of symbolic
link to create.
If the target exists and is a directory, create a
directory symbolic link.
Otherwise, create a file symbolic link.

.TP
\fB\-t\fP, \fB\-\-target-directory\fP
Treat DIRECTORY as the directory in which to create
links based on the remaining arguments.

.TP
\fB\-T\fP, \fB\-\-no-target-directory\fP
Treat LINKNAME as a normal file always.

.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Show brief help message.

.TP
\fB\-\-version\fP
Display version information

.SH NOT\ IMPLEMENTED
.B winln
does not implement the following
command line arguments from GNU ln(1):
.br
\fB-b\fP, \fB--backup\fP,
\fB-i\fP, \fB--interactive\fP,
\fB-L\fP, \fB--logical\fP,
\fB-n\fP, \fB--no-dereference\fP,
\fB-P\fP, \fB--physical\fP

